<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Dear Mr. Kramer
</h4>

<p>
Somehow, I think this post is very similar to what was written on many surveys slipped into that cardboard box on the  information table. It's certainly quite like the one I dropped in Sunday afternoon. <br />
<br />
At some point, newspaper writers started doing narrative every day, and many of us are coming to Nieman to learn more about how to do what we do better. Staff writers from the New Yorker and authors who get years to work on books can help us with craft and technique, if they can stop focusing on their product long enough to talk about their process. But what's more helpful are the people who do what we do, and who can talk about how they do what they do and what they think about it.<br />
<br />
Us daily folks? We're hungry, Mr. Kramer. Feed us.
</p>
